# Vertical Templates

## Applies when

Editing `context/verticals/` — niche archetype definitions for Copy and Design agents.

Shared context invariants: `30-context-files`. Design-system components: `31-design-system`.

## Source of truth

- [PRD.md](PRD.md) §7.2 (`content.json` — `vertical`, `sections`).
- [PRD.md](PRD.md) §11 (`context/verticals/*.md`).
- Schema: `schemas/content.schema.json` when present.
- C `22-agent-copy` (fills slots), C `23-agent-design` (maps slots → template HTML).

## Required behavior

- **One niche per file**: e.g. `construction.md` — not a universal template for all niches.
- **Document per vertical**:
  - Niche signals (keywords, audience, typical services)
  - `vertical` id matching filename (e.g. `construction` → `construction.md`)
  - Section order and slot names
  - Recommended copy tone hints (reference `tone-of-voice.md`, do not duplicate)
- **Slot alignment (mandatory)**: slots MUST match `content.json` sections:
  - `hero` (eyebrow, headline, subheadline, cta)
  - `trust[]` (title, text) — min 3
  - `symptoms[]` (pain, solve) — min 4
  - `why_us[]` (title, text) — min 3
  - `contact` (phone, cta)
- **`vertical` field**: value in `content.json` must match template id/filename.
- **Milestone 3 first vertical**: one complete archetype (`construction`) — not a stub. This pipeline is construction-only.
- **Paired HTML** (optional): vertical may reference design-system component layout for Design agent.

## When user requests forbidden pattern

- «Vertical без привязки к content.json» → stop; slots must match PRD §7.2 / schema.
- «Generic vertical universal.md для всех ниш» → stop; niche-specific archetype required.
- «Добавь секцию без обновления content.schema» → stop; `01-contract-first`.
- «Смешай 3 ниши в одном файле» → stop; one niche per vertical file.

## Forbidden behavior

- Do not define slots absent from `content.json` / `content.schema.json`.
- Do not write English-only vertical docs unless user requests.
- Do not mix multiple niches in one template file.
- Do not store lead-specific copy in vertical templates — templates are archetypes, not client data.

## Output requirements

- `.md` (and optional HTML reference) per vertical under `context/verticals/`.
- Slot list explicitly documents mapping to `content.json` sections.

## Verification checklist

- [ ] Every slot in vertical exists in PRD `content.json` example.
- [ ] `vertical` id consistent with filename.
- [ ] One niche per file; first vertical complete for milestone 3.
- [ ] Copy agent can fill slots; Design agent can map to template.
- [ ] New sections require schema + PRD update first.
